{"text": "FEDERAL\nTRADE\nCOMMISSION\n\nWASHINGTON, D. C. 20580\n\nFor further information call:\nDavid H. Buswell\nOffice of Publ.\n(202) 962-7144\n\nInformation\n\nFOR RELEASE After 8:30 A.M., Thursday, October 1, 1970\n\nPTC DIRECTS TOBACCO. INDUSTRY TO SUBMIT SPECIFICS\nON DISCLOSING TAR AND NICOTINE CONTENT\n\nThe Federal Trade Commission has given cigarette manufacturers 30 days in which\n\nto tell the Conmission exactly how they voluntarily intend to disclose tar and nicotine\ncontent in cigarette advertising. The FIC also postponed the October 15 hearings on\nits proposed trade regulation rule to require such disclosure.\n\nThe Commission, after considering the tobacco industry's plan, will set a new\nhearing date if it still feels a trade regulation rule would be in the public interest.\n\nFIC Chairman Miles W. Kirkpatrick said: \"The Commission's objective is te insure\nthat all cigarette advertising make these tar and nicotine disclosures as soon as\nPossible. If the industry can devise a voluntary plan that is feasible and appropriate,\nthe Commission is willing to consider it. A trade regulation rule, if contested in the\ncourts, might take a long time to become effective; a vorkable, voluntary plan by the\nindustry could be put into effect innediately.\n\nThe written submissions by the industry will be placed on the public record for\n30 days for public comment.\n\noe\n\n6TLZeTTO", "words": [{"text": "FEDERAL", "x0": 318, "y0": 136, "x1": 396, "y1": 158, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "TRADE", "x0": 336, "y0": 162, "x1": 395, "y1": 184, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "COMMISSION", "x0": 277, "y0": 188, "x1": 395, "y1": 211, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "WASHINGTON,", "x0": 314, "y0": 285, "x1": 401, "y1": 300, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "D.", "x0": 406, "y0": 287, "x1": 414, "y1": 296, "conf": 41.0}, {"text": "C.", "x0": 422, "y0": 287, "x1": 429, "y1": 296, "conf": 69.0}, {"text": "20580", "x0": 437, "y0": 287, "x1": 471, "y1": 297, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "For", "x0": 475